    tip: "Before you write, say your main idea in one sentence to a friend. If you can't, you're not ready to write the paragraph. Afterward, read each sentence and ask: does this support my topic sentence? If not, cut it or move it.",
    note: "American schools often teach the *hamburger paragraph*: the topic and concluding sentences are the bun, and the supporting details are the filling. In emails and online writing, Americans use much shorter paragraphs, often just two or three sentences, because they're easier to read on a screen.",
